rep("<strong>Price leader/follower pricing</strong> is used in an oligopolistic market", '<p><strong>Price leader/follower pricing</strong> is used in an oligopolistic market, where a few firms can observe one another\'s pricing. The firm with the largest market share acts as price leader and sets the industry price. Some years ago Kellogg\'s, joining Kraft, Campbell, and Hershey, announced a 2% increase across many brands, and General Mills and Post were expected to follow (alongside <em>shrinkflation</em>—keeping package size while cutting contents). Because every rival moves in step, relative positions are unchanged and the only real change is that consumers pay more.</p>')
